## Protocol (generated — edit the repo, not this block)

Rules live in `~/.agents/rules/`: git-workflow, code-quality,
completion-standard, agent-style, karpathy-guidelines.

Enforcement is real, not advisory. Hooks block violations by rule ID; the index
is in `GITHUB-RULES.md`. When a block fires, fix the cause — working around it
is itself a violation. `PROTOCOL_OVERRIDE=<rule-id>` waives one rule for one
command and only from a human shell.

- 1 issue → 1 branch → 1 PR. Agents open PRs and never merge; @OWNER@ merges.
- Identity comes from `~/.agents/protocol.conf`. Never hardcode a name or
  address in a tracked file.
- Response style is owned by the caveman plugin. Change it with
  `/caveman lite|full|ultra`, not by adding a hook.
